    "created_at": "2018-05-18T15:16:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-18T15:16:16Z",
    "body": "For what it's worth. I think the null issue is not really an issue: the dictionary Gecko uses here for some reason declared the members as nullable, and if they are not nullable we should simply remove those `?` from the dictionary members.\r\n\r\nThe ordering thing is still there.  We can hack our implementation to get the current spec ordering if need be, but it would be extra code and cognitive overhead, obviously.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
